+> STOP. Captain's notes: non-binding. Captain writes, Captain trims. Anyone else: close this file now.
+
+# Captain Notes
+
+Binding behaviour lives in `.feature` specs and referenced `assets/**`. History lives in git. These notes carry only what the next cycle needs.
+
+## Acceptance-suite defects pinned (TodomVC shakedown)
+
+The fixed Cypress browser acceptance suite reports 8 failures. Two clusters; both are real
+product defects, not test errors.
+
+### Cluster B — persisted filter overrides the live hash (failures 6, 7, 8)
+`currentFilter()` reads the persisted `todos-vanilla-filter` key BEFORE `location.hash`, so
+after navigating to a filter and back to All, the stale persisted filter wins. Reproducible in
+the happy-dom harness. Pinned by three behaviour scenarios in `features/todos-routing.feature`
+under `Rule: Filter follows the live hash, not the persisted filter`. They fail now
+(`3 failed`): wrong visible count after returning to All, and `All` filter link not `selected`.
+
+### Cluster A — list render destroys node identity (failures 1, 2, 3, 4)
+`render()` clears `list.innerHTML` and rebuilds every `<li>` on each state change. A real
+browser holds a node reference across the click, then finds it detached (`cy.eq`/`cy.find`
+detached). happy-dom re-queries per access and cannot see this, so it is browser-only. Pinned
+by a source-level `@conformance` scenario in `features/todos-item.feature`
+(`The list render preserves the identity of unchanged item nodes`). QM implements the bespoke
+source-level checker for the `list-render stability seam`: it must fail while `render` clears
+and recreates item nodes, and pass once the app mutates existing nodes in place.
+
+### Cluster C — edit mode hides other controls (failure 5)
+Entering edit mode adds `.editing` and focuses, but never hides the item's `.view`
+(toggle + label). No CSS exists, so a real browser keeps the toggle visible. Browser-only
+visual concern. Pinned by a source-level `@conformance` scenario in
+`features/todos-editing.feature` (`Entering edit mode hides the item's view controls`). QM
+implements the `edit-mode visibility seam` checker: fail while edit mode leaves the view
+controls visible; pass once edit mode hides them.
+
+## Watchbill
+`watchbill.json` lists all five pinned scenarios under `watch1`. They are the QM targets.
+
+## Next role
+QM. Base commit is HEAD. Context MUST clear before QM per the Captain to QM bulkhead. QM builds
+the two bespoke conformance checkers for the `@conformance` scenarios; Crew fixes the product
+(app-side) so a real browser passes. Captain writes no production code.
